    {
      "title": "Book Review - \"Sweet Bean Paste\" - Sci-fi Fantasy Lit Chick",
      "snippet": "Thematically, Sweet Bean Paste focuses on the benefits to friendship and in being honest with ourselves and others. Sentaro tends to keep things to himself and doesn't like socializing, with Tokue treats their shop's customers as people with lives and troubles of their own, and she's never too busy to not lend a compassionate ear.",
      "link": "scififantasylitchick.wordpress.com/2025/07/01/book-review-sweet-bean-paste/"
    },
    {
      "title": "Book Review: Sweet Bean Paste — A Book That Invites You To Listen",
      "snippet": "Durian Sukegawa's Sweet Bean Paste (originally An) is one of those rare novels that moves you with its silence as much as its words. It's a tender meditation on purpose, connection, and what it means to live a meaningful life—even when the world refuses to see your worth. The story unfolds like the slow, patient rhythm of making dorayaki: deliberate, humble, and yet full of quiet grace ...",
      "link": "booksandus.com/sweet-bean-paste-review/"
